        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Quadr II 8d" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="545" ed="#liebermann"/>Rogerius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#QuadrII_8d.lnote.oe.9"/> uero Saresberiensis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#QuadrII_8d.lnote.oe.10"/> electus episcopus, uir multa bene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#QuadrII_8d.lnote.oe.11"/> meritorum precipuitate sollempnis, sanctum ipsius archiepiscopi reditum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#QuadrII_8d.lnote.oe.12"/> iustis desideriis expectauit, in tanta rerum perturbatione sollicitus, ut unicuique<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="ff" target="#QuadrII_8d.lnote.oe.ff"/> debita diligenter ac fideliter intimaret.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 545 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
